1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:17,158
Delhi, October 2026. Eleven days of bus GPS, 2.5 million tickets.

2
00:00:17,158 --> 00:00:32,300
3,688 stations. 2,403 routes. 803,764 travel-time profiles.

3
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:42,610
Type three letters. The station list resolves as you type.

4
00:00:42,610 --> 00:00:58,665
Kashmere Gate to Nehru Place, 08:30 on a Thursday.

5
00:00:58,665 --> 00:01:28,660
Every line is routed on the real OpenStreetMap Delhi road network.

6
00:01:28,660 --> 00:01:39,591
2D and 3D. The route is drawn beneath the buildings, never over them.

7
00:01:39,591 --> 00:01:51,129
Rank by fastest, balanced, or calmer.

8
00:01:51,129 --> 00:02:04,579
The same trip, every hour. 23 to 37 minutes.

9
00:02:04,579 --> 00:02:23,639
Crowding along a route, from ticketing data. A relative index, never occupancy.

10
00:02:23,639 --> 00:02:46,380
22.4 s segment error against 41.6 s for the timetable.

11
00:02:46,380 --> 00:02:58,702
Delhi Bus Intelligence — Transport Stack Hackathon 2026.
